 with gusts up to 70-75 mph for the\nnorthern Front Range mountains and foothills. West 20 to 30 mph\nwith gusts up to 50 mph on the plains.\n\n* RELATIVE HUMIDITY...Between 10 to 20 percent.\n\n* IMPACTS...Conditions will be favorable for rapid fire spread. Avoid\noutdoor burning and any activity that may produce a spark and start\na wildfire.","ends":"2026-11-18T16:00:00-07:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Larimer and Boulder Counties Between 6000 and 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Central and South Weld County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.382bc923e46a867f01f5d73980c813cffc84cd48.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.382bc923e46a867f01f5d73980c813cffc84cd48.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-11-17T17:53:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KBOU 171753 AFDBOU Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Denver/Boulder CO 1053 AM MST Tue Nov 17 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Locally dense fog across the plains this morning, mainly in Weld and Morgan counties. - First wind event of the season likely for the northern Front Range mountains and foothills Tuesday night into Wednesday. A few gusts up to 75 mph plausible. - Elevated","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=BOU&issuedby=BOU&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"BOU","issued":"2026-11-17T10:17:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION...Today through Saturday...Southwest flow aloft will increase today ahead of a storm system. Breezy southwest winds develop this afternoon, mainly over the mountains and for areas south of I-76. A Denver cyclone forms bringing east to northeast winds north of I-76 and limits mixing to marginal and poor. Elsewhere, smoke dispersion is expected reach fair to good. Winds increase late ton","url":"https://forecast.weather.go